title: Grid movement
intro: A player that steps tile by tile on a tilemap, blocked by its walls, with no code: for puzzle games, roguelikes and old-school RPGs.
project: Empty | Grid Steps

chapter: A room to walk in | A tilemap, a rock and a grid player
create: Tilemap
rename: Level
set: Tilemap.Tiles = 11111111\n1......1\n1.11...1\n1......1\n11111111
select: Main Camera
set: Transform.Position.X = 4
set: Transform.Position.Y = -2.5
look: 4, -2.5, 4
say: Here's a small room painted on a tilemap: walls all round, and a wall in the middle.
deselect
create: Sprite
rename: Rock
set: Transform.Position.X = 6.5
set: Transform.Position.Y = -3.5
add: BoxCollider
say: And a rock with a collider, in the bottom right corner.
deselect
create: Grid Player
set: Transform.Position.X = 1.4
set: Transform.Position.Y = -1.6
explain: menu:Entity | Entity, Create Grid Player | The Entity menu has a new player: Create Grid Player.
explain: component:GridMovement | Grid Movement | It's a box with a body and a collider, like the other players, and a Grid Movement instead of running and jumping.
explain: field:GridMovement.StepTime | Step Time | Each press steps it one cell of the tilemap, gliding there in this many seconds.
explain: field:GridMovement.RepeatDelay | Repeat and Repeat Delay | Holding a way keeps it walking, straight away or after a pause, which suits careful puzzle steps.
explain: field:GridMovement.Diagonal | Diagonal and Stay On Map | It moves four ways, or diagonally too, and stays on the map even where there's no wall.

chapter: Step by step | Walls and solid things stop it
play
wait: 0.5
expectat: Player = 1.5, -1.5
say: It's placed a little off, so it starts on the middle of its cell.
tap: Right
wait: 0.4
tap: Right
wait: 0.4
expectat: Player = 3.5, -1.5
say: Each tap is one step, one cell at a time.
hold: Down 0.6
wait: 0.3
expectat: Player = 3.5, -1.5
explain: game | Blocked | Below it is the wall in the middle, so it just turns to face it. A bump sound can play here, once a press.
hold: Right 1
wait: 0.3
expectat: Player = 6.5, -1.5
say: Holding a way keeps it walking, until the wall on the right stops it.
hold: Down 1
wait: 0.3
expectat: Player = 6.5, -2.5
explain: game | The rock | Solid colliders stop it too, like this rock, and so do other grid movers. Coins, doors and other triggers don't, so it picks things up as it steps onto them.
stop
say: That's grid movement, with no code. Scripts can step it too, and it works in network games, with each player stepping their own.
